jev-duum
Copyright 2026 jev-duum contributors

Adapter code is adapted from laya-duum, which controls the pure-Python Duum
engine with the Laya decision model:
https://github.com/hadlock/laya-duum
Copyright laya-duum contributors. Licensed under Apache-2.0.

Changes: the local Laya Core ML / torch decision backend is replaced by a
remote TypeSafe System One (Jev) HTTP client. One request per decision carries
the three choice questions against a single combined state; token accounting,
cost reporting and per-question confidence recording are added; the engine
adapter, canonical snapshot, deterministic assistance, fixed-tick scheduling,
recording and replay layers are unchanged.

No model weights are included in this repository: Jev is a remote API, and the
adapter ships only standard-library HTTP code. This is an independent project,
not an official Convai Innovations, Apple or TypeSafe release.

